const HALTS = "HALT CONDITIONS (owner-set). On ANY of these: STOP, commit nothing further, report.\n\n1. Any change under apps/core/ - the server module is frozen for this pipeline. A screen that\n   cannot be built without a server change is a PLAN DEFECT report, not a server edit.\n2. A required-DIED mutant that SURVIVES because the SHIPPED CODE IS WRONG (branch (a) above).\n3. Any file outside your task's Files list in the plan.\n4. Any frozen-path edit.\n5. Any new dependency, env var, or CI edit.\n6. Any instruction - INCLUDING a reviewer's correction - to amend or force-push PUSHED history.\n   Refuse it and report that you refused. (A commit you have not yet pushed is yours to amend.)\n7. Scope drift toward corporate/TPA contract billing, e-invoicing/IRP, PSP APIs, IPD deposit\n   policy, or collections automation. The patient dues worklist and the advance instrument are the\n   whole allowance.\n8. Any attempt to 'align' the two owner-ratified error-body conventions. Billing uses the\n   OPD-shaped body { statusCode, message, code, detail? }; patients and tariff keep theirs."

const CARRIED = "CARRIED FORWARD FROM PIPELINES A AND B - READ ALL OF IT, IT IS ABOUT THE API YOU ARE CALLING\n\nFull detail in plans/reports/plan-08-pipeline-B-notes.md sections 3, 4 and 6. The items that bind\nevery task in this pipeline:\n\n1. **TWO REFUSALS ARE TERMINAL BY DESIGN. RENDER THEM AS DEAD ENDS.** Once an advance-refund\n   voucher has returned a receipt's money, that receipt can never be marked entered-in-error\n   (`eie_advance_refunded`) and its money can never be allocated (`allocation_exceeds_advance`).\n   There is NO correction path, deliberately: a paid voucher is cash that physically left the\n   drawer. Both answer 409 with detail { askedPaise?, wouldBeAdvancePaise, refundedPaise }. A screen\n   that offers a remedial action here would be lying to the cashier.\n\n2. **THE CLEARANCE-DISCOUNT LANE IS DEAD BY DEFAULT ON A FRESH ENVIRONMENT.** `credit-notes.ts`\n   treats an absent `manualCaps[category]` as a cap of ZERO, and `seed-billing.ts` seeds no tariff\n   adjustment-rule cap rows at all, so every clearance ask is refused `over_cap` until an admin\n   creates a cap row through the tariff module. Render that refusal as a CONFIGURATION message, not\n   as a money refusal - a cashier told 'over cap' on a cap of zero will file a bug.\n\n3. **DO NOT ADD A THIRD COPY OF THE OPD FEE BRANCH.** There are already two in the server and they\n   disagree (a mutant proved it survives the shipped suite 14/14). Read the fee over HTTP from\n   `GET /billing/visits/:encounterId/fee-quote` and render what it returns.\n\n4. **`GET /billing/receipts` RETURNS THE RAW RECEIPTS ROW, INCLUDING `panNumber`** (the Rule 114B\n   PAN captured above the 50,000 threshold), behind `billing.invoice.read` - a permission the\n   module's README grants to every cashier. `GET /billing/refunds` likewise returns raw\n   `payeeName`/`payeeIdType`/`payeeIdRef`. **This is a SERVER defect and pipeline C cannot fix it**\n   (apps/core is frozen). What you MUST do: never render PAN or payee identity refs on a screen,\n   select only the fields your screen needs out of the response, and RESTATE the exposure in your\n   report so it stays visible. Do not let a screen that quietly drops the field read as a fix - the\n   screen is not the security boundary, and a cashier can still call the route directly.\n\n5. **NEITHER `GET /billing/receipts` NOR `GET /billing/sessions` HAS PAGINATION OR A DATE WINDOW**,\n   and `listDues` filters in memory. Known scale seams at Phase-1 volumes. Do not build paging the\n   API cannot serve, and do not assume a bounded response.\n\n6. **`advance.received` CARRIES A correlationId WHEN `issueInvoice` EMITS IT (overpayment surplus)\n   AND NONE WHEN `recordReceipt` EMITS IT (standalone advance)** - one event name, two envelope\n   shapes. Correct per the plan's 'where one exists' rule; a consumer keying on correlationId will\n   see a hole.\n\n7. **THE BACK-OFFICE DAY BOOK SHOULD READ `dayBook` LIVE** rather than the stored\n   `daily_closes.totals`, which are computed outside the idempotent claim transaction and can\n   permanently omit a document that committed in that window.\n\n8. **`d3074fa` IS NOT A PRECEDENT.** It edited a byte-frozen OPD controller as an owner-ratified,\n   one-line, disclosed follow-up. It does not license touching frozen OPD or core files here."

