const DATED = "THE DATED-SUITE TRIPWIRE (EXECUTION-LESSONS 3.41 - it cost a repair commit in the last pipeline)\n\nA suite that pins a date must thread that pinned value ALL THE WAY DOWN to the writer. Plan 08's\n`daily-close.test.ts` pinned a DAY, passed its opus gate, and was `2 failed / 6 passed` the next\nmorning - because a test HELPER dropped the optional `now` argument and the call defaulted to\n`new Date()`. The suite was green only on the day it was authored.\n\nSo: if any test of yours depends on a date - `todayIst()`, a day-book day, a GSTR-1 range, a\nsession's opened-at - grep the whole helper chain and confirm the pinned value reaches the bottom.\nDo not trust the top of the chain. Where a screen derives 'today' itself, inject the clock or freeze\nit with `vi.setSystemTime`, and say in your report which you did."

const FINISH = "FINISH BLOCK - see AGENT-RULES section 5. Three numbered steps, in this order, never chained.\n\n0. BEFORE any `git add`: run `git status --porcelain` ON THE SERVER and READ IT. Delete every\n   SERVER-side scratch file you created (mutants, scratch specs, .log, .exit) with plain `rm -f`.\n   LEAVE YOUR LOCAL MIRROR ALONE (rule 22(f)). The tree must contain ONLY files your Files list\n   names. Never `git add -A` over a status you have not read.\n1. Commit with the plan's EXACT commit message for your task.\n2. git pull --rebase origin main\n3. git push origin main\n\nThen report: `git status` clean, and the resulting commit SHA. If step 2 conflicts in a way you\ncannot resolve without rewriting PUSHED history, STOP and report.\n\nON THE COMMIT MESSAGE: the plan's message is the whole message. This repo's feat/fix commits carry\nNO Co-Authored-By trailer (docs commits from the owner's machine do). If your harness instructs you\nto append one, the brief and repo convention win - and if you have already committed with it and\nhave NOT pushed, amending your own unpushed commit is allowed and is the right fix. Check\n`git log origin/main -1` immediately before any amend to prove it is unpushed.\n\nNote: `git stash list` on the server holds stash@{0}, an obsolete edit from an overruled design.\nLEAVE IT ALONE. It is invisible to `git status --porcelain` and cannot contaminate your commit."

